  "problem": "The graph of $y=5f(3x-6)+2,$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\text{T}1)$ - Translate right by $6$ units\n\n- $(\\text{T}2)$ - Stretch by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}3)$ - Translate up by $2$ units\n\n- $(\\text{T}4)$ - Stretch by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}5)$ - Translate right by $2$ units\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?",
